================================================================================================
WHAT THIS MEANS FOR QUOTED POSTERIORS
================================================================================================
  Not one chain in this tree has ever recorded R-1 at or below its own stopping target.
  Every posterior the corpus quotes -- epsilon ~ 1.24%, H0 = 69.9 and 69.05, S8 = 0.823,
  z_on, xi = 0.142, the alpha_c band -- is therefore read off an unconverged instrument.

  That does not make the numbers wrong. A chain far from R-1 = 0.05 can still have a
  well-located mode, and several of these are quoted as best-fit points rather than as
  interval estimates, which is a much weaker claim and survives.

  What it does mean is that INTERVALS from these chains carry no width guarantee, and
  intervals are exactly what the band was used as. The distinction the corpus needs is
  between a quoted POINT (defensible, and usually what is meant) and a quoted WIDTH
  (not defensible from any chain in this tree), and it is not currently drawn anywhere.
